#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060657} :activity/id #uuid "d6d1f64b-2ca1-5bc1-b04e-f255dfa6a0e3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049043 :topic/id #uuid "d57b5ff8-115f-5129-8276-a2c829ed83ca" :topic/math-academy-id 154} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060657 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060933 :tutorial/content "We can calculate the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ using the following five-step algorithm.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant $\\det(A)$ of the matrix.\n\n**Step 2:** Form the **matrix $M$ of the minors** of $A,$ where each entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ is replaced by its minor $M_{ij}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & {M}_{12} & {M}_{13} \\\\ {M}_{21} & {M}_{22} & {M}_{23} \\\\ {M}_{31} & {M}_{32} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the **matrix $C$ of cofactors** by changing the sign of some entries of the matrix of the minors according to the **rule of alternating signs**:\n   \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}+ & - & + \\\\ - & + & - \\\\ + & - & +\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFor each entry of $M$, we change the sign if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$-$\". Otherwise, if the corresponding sign in the pattern is \"$+$\", then we don't change the entry.\n\nSo, the matrix of cofactors is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & -{M}_{12} & {M}_{13} \\\\ -{M}_{21} & {M}_{22} & -{M}_{23} \\\\ {M}_{31} & -{M}_{32} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors, $C^T.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{M}_{11} & -{M}_{21} & {M}_{31} \\\\ -{M}_{12} & {M}_{22} & -{M}_{32} \\\\ {M}_{13} & -{M}_{23} & {M}_{33}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix:\n   \n\n$$\nA^{-1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det ( A)}C^{T}\n$$\n\nIn other words, we divide each entry of the transpose of the matrix of cofactors by the determinant of the original matrix (which we computed in step 1).\n\nLet's see this in practice, in the next example." :tutorial/id #uuid "9c7ba5cd-b4b2-595b-bbad-dfbdac248280" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3051 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "40317ef1-e2cc-5e12-bdbe-2a42b66c8d16" :step/math-academy-id 16475 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060658}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060658 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059754 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059563 :question/id #uuid "8cd94856-fbe5-53a4-b7f2-f5b29b7aa927" :question/math-academy-id "e-4514"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50c01507-99a7-5328-8d74-c9e9bda51330" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050727}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060458} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240804} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299747} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299749} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299750} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299753} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362383} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386055} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393292}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Matrix of Cofactors"} :step/id #uuid "fc1a94a9-263e-5e41-a86c-15959c3a9e6e" :step/math-academy-id 16476 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060660}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060659 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059755 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059564 :question/id #uuid "9180ff3b-46d2-5df7-81b6-ac75bef51e00" :question/math-academy-id "e-4515"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d79fb5d1-22a6-511d-90ca-7d66c540d172" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050383}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060450} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060459} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240876} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240877} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240878} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292886} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292887} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299761} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299762} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299764} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299765} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299801} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299809} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299812} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342006} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342008} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342009} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362389} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362402} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382256}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cofactor Method To Solve for an Unknown Quantity"} :step/id #uuid "902e05e9-d18d-5cea-b49d-e1ac3fd78059" :step/math-academy-id 16477} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060660 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060934 :tutorial/content "We make the matrix $C$ of cofactors by changing the sign of alternate entries of the matrix $M$ of the minors. So, each entry $c_{ij}$ of $C$ equals\n\n$$\nc_{ij} = (-1)^{i+j} M_{ij},\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the minor of the entry $a_{ij}$ in the matrix $A.$\n\nWith this and the formula for the inverse, we can write the formula for each entry $a'_{ij}$ of the inverse matrix $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n$$\na'_{ij} = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)}c^t_{ij}\n        = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)} c_{ji}\n$$\n\nHere, we used the fact that the entry $c^t_{ij}$ of $C^T$ is equal to the entry $c_{ji}$ of $C$ by the definition of the transpose." :tutorial/id #uuid "835c9ab0-dbce-5297-9a57-3978df178fa3" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3052 :tutorial/title "Calculating Individual Entries of the Matrix of Cofactors"} :step/id #uuid "b8784f82-7077-5c6e-b26b-f9e36420e73c" :step/math-academy-id 16478 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060661}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059756 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059565 :question/id #uuid "26e9a55f-7711-5d8f-ab0a-e8638f2d2dec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4516"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c704e019-035f-5807-b02d-62b9cd44c1c7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050163}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060153} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060154} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240871} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240874} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287826} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287827} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287828} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287829} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287830} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287832} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287833} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292885} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299754} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299756} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299757} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299758} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299776} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299777} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299778}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Element of the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "cb81629b-755e-56a7-88e6-963569b9be54" :step/math-academy-id 16479 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060659}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Inverse of a 3x3 Matrix Using the Cofactor Method" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059887}]}
